menu "Debugging"

config NEKOBOX_DEBUG
	bool "Numbers about the user interface and the self tests"
	default y
	help
	  The frame rate of a swiped list and the time a screen takes to its first picture are
	  printed when they happen.

config NEKOBOX_SELFTEST
	bool "Play the default video and seek, pause and change the volume by itself"
	depends on NEKOBOX_DEBUG && NEKOBOX_FEATURE_VIDEO
	help
	  For a check without touching the screen: the steps and the positions are printed.

config NEKOBOX_THEME_TEST
	bool "Switch the settings by itself and print the result (ends with PASS or FAIL)"
	depends on NEKOBOX_DEBUG && NEKOBOX_FEATURE_SETTINGS
	help
	  Theme, brightness, saved passwords, a Wi-Fi scan and joining the saved network, and
	  starting and leaving a game, for the features that are built.

config NEKOBOX_SOAK
	bool "Play every video and game on the card, twice, and print the free memory after each"
	depends on NEKOBOX_DEBUG
	help
	  Finds memory that is not given back: the largest block and the free memory in total
	  of the malloc arena are printed before the first file and after every one. Ends with PASS
	  or FAIL.

config NEKOBOX_RADIO_TEST
	bool "Start the Wi-Fi chip, scan and stop it again several times, and print the free memory"
	depends on NEKOBOX_DEBUG && NEKOBOX_FEATURE_NET
	help
	  Checks that the driver can be shut down completely and started again: after every stop the
	  memory of the driver must be back in the arena. Ends with PASS or FAIL.

config NEKOBOX_PROFILE
	bool "Sample where the game thread spends its time and print the busiest code blocks"
	depends on NEKOBOX_DEBUG && NEKOBOX_FEATURE_GAMES
	help
	  20 seconds after a game starts, 6000 samples of the program counter are taken (one a
	  millisecond) and the busiest 64 byte blocks are printed as "prof <address> <count>".

endmenu
